    "result": "I implemented `order_total` in `solution.py` following all seven rules in `spec.md`. I also wrote 8 tests in `tests/test_solution.py`, and they all pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`.\n\nThe tests cover these cases:\n- **Empty order:** subtotal and shipping are both 0.\n- **Shipping:** the 100.00 threshold, applied to the subtotal after the discount.\n- **Item validation:** bad quantities and negative prices raise `ValueError`.\n- **Coupons:** percent and fixed discounts, with the fixed discount capped at the subtotal.\n- **Coupon errors:** expiry on and after the `expires` date, used codes, the `min_subtotal` boundary, and an unknown `kind` all behave as the spec says.\n- **Coupon values:** bad percent and fixed values raise `ValueError`.\n- **Rounding:** halves round up.\n\nOne call the spec didn't settle: I reject a `bool` as a quantity, even though `True` is technically an `int`.",
